! mcp_bootstrap_p15.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 15.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.22, header "PAGE NUMBER 15".
! docs/boot_plan.md M3.
!
! THIS IS WHERE THE BOOTSTRAP HANDS OFF.  Printed p.14's last
! instruction is "B,X 10", and X 10 is line 17 of THIS page, at
! 000622.00.  Every other MCP page transcribed so far is bootstrap;
! this is the first page of MCP proper.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE IS TWO THINGS AND ONLY THE SECOND ASSEMBLES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-6 are punch control -- PUNFUL, two (CC*)DD card images
! (the "HED,REP,11C11IPL,LOAD,," header card and an 11C11IPL
! trailer), PUNORG, "PUNID,11C11IPL" and RESEQ.  They change what
! STRAP punches, not what it assembles, which is why printed
! pp.3-15 and pp.16+ are ONE assembly punching TWO decks (see
! mcp_bootstrap_p13.strap's header).  The two card images DO move
! the location counter -- the listing prints 000621.00 for line 2
! and 000631.34 for line 3 -- and line 7, "SLC,X BS END", puts it
! straight back to 000621.00, so the card images are overlaid by
! the code that follows and nothing of them survives.  This deck
! starts at the SLC for that reason.
!
! Line 14's CNOP is a no-op here: 000621.00 is already a word
! boundary.  It is transcribed as the listing prints it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT MCP INITIALIZATION DOES, lines 15-26
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "MOVE COMMUNICATION REGION TO IPL AREA AND POSITION DISK".  The
! bootstrap has left the whole MCP image in a buffer at X BUFER;
! initialization computes how far into that buffer the communication
! region sits ($9), copies the region down to S MCP, patches the
! machine's own size into it, copies MCP itself into storage at the
! address LVE fetched into $8, and then LOCATEs the disk to arc zero.
!
! Lines 15-16 are two BE instructions used as DATA, not as branches.
! "X IN  BE,X IN END-X IN" assembles an address field of 004645 and
! the comment calls it "SIZE OF IPL FOR UPDATE PROGRAM"; "X UPDAT
! BE,0" is "NUMBER OF PROSA ARCS", a slot something later fills.
! The opcode byte prints 00 for both, which is BE's own code -- a
! word of data that would branch if it were ever executed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! AND THE PAGE ENDS AT THE DISK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 26 is "LOC(SEOP),0.0,0.0  -POSITION TO ARC ZERO" and lines
! 28-33 are the "DISK IO TEST": three SIC/branch pairs testing
! exchange error (EKJ), unit not ready (UNRJ) and channel busy
! (CBJ).  So transcribing this page does NOT make the boot run
! further on today's model -- it converts "halts at PC 0, one word
! past X BS END" into "stops at a LOCATE, wanting a 7612/353".
! That is the point of reading it: this is the page that says
! exactly which device has to answer next, and what it is asked.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS, and how each value is justified
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   X IN END  printed p.98 line 36  "X IN END SYN,$"       005466.00
!             -- and line 15 of this page corroborates it: 0o621 +
!                0o4645 = 0o5466.
!   X BUFER   printed p.13 line 38  "SYN,X IN END+2000.0"  011406.00
!             -- printed verbatim in lines 19, 20, 21 and 24 here.
!   X S ROOF  printed p.13 line 26  "X S ROOF  XW,0"       000546.00
!   X ERR AD  printed p.13 line 37  "X ERR AD  VF,0"       000551.00
!   X ERROR   printed p.5  line 5   "X ERROR LX,$2,X ERR IN" 000133.00
!
! >>> S MCP AND S ROOF ARE READ OFF THIS PAGE'S OWN BINARY OUTPUT,
! >>> NOT OFF A DEFINITION.  They are communication-region symbols
! and the page that defines them has not been transcribed.  Line
! 21's second half-word prints 002150.00 20, whose address field is
! S MCP; line 23 prints 002162.01 70, whose address field is S ROOF
! (bit 23 is what distinguishes SR from LR -- line 22's LR prints
! the same opcode byte 70 with bit 23 clear).  So:
!       S MCP  = 002150.00,  S ROOF = 002162.00
! That is a value taken from a listing's own output, which is the
! weakest kind of evidence this project accepts, and it is recorded
! as such: when the communication-region page is transcribed, these
! two SYNs must be checked against it, and a disagreement is a real
! finding, not a typo.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE INDICATOR NUMBERS CHECK, three ways
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 29, 31 and 33 print 000133.03 46, 000133.03 C6 and
! 000133.04 46.  Reading the indicator field as bits 19-24 gives
! 000110 = 6, 000111 = 7 and 001000 = 8, which are EKJ, UNRJ and
! CBJ in opcodes.py's INDICATOR_BITS -- the three the comments name
! ("IF EXCHANGE ERROR", "IF DISK NOT READY", "IF DISK BUSY").  The
! branch address is the same 000133.00 in all three, which is
! X ERROR, known independently from printed p.5.  Three independent
! agreements on one row group.
XINEND  SYN, (8)5466.0
XBUFER  SYN, (8)11406.0
XSROOF  SYN, (8)546.0
XERRAD  SYN, (8)551.0
XERROR  SYN, (8)133.0
SMCP    SYN, (8)2150.0     ! read off line 21's binary output
SROOF   SYN, (8)2162.0     ! read off line 23's binary output

        SLC, (8)621.0      ! line 7  "SLC,X BS END"
        CNOP               ! line 14 -- already on a word boundary

! ---- MCP INITIALIZATION -------------------------------------------
XIN     BE, XINEND-XIN              ! line 15 -SIZE OF IPL FOR UPDATE
XUPDAT  BE, 0                       ! line 16 -NUMBER OF PROSA ARCS
X10     LVS, $9, $12, $11, $14      ! line 17 -COMPUTE NUMBER OF WORDS
                                    !          PRECEEDING MCP
        LVE, $8, XBUFER($9)         ! line 19 - GET (MCP)
X101    LC, $0, XBUFER+.32($9)      ! line 20 -GET SIZE OF COMM REGION
        T,   0, XBUFER($9), SMCP    ! line 21 -MOVE COMM REGION
                                    !   listing "T,$0,X BUFER($9),S MCP"
        LR, $0, XSROOF              ! line 22
        SR, $0, SROOF               ! line 23 -PLACE 7030 SIZE IN COMM
        T,  10, XBUFER($9), 0.0($8) ! line 24 -PLACE MCP IN STORAGE
                                    !   listing "T,$10,X BUFER($9),0.0($8)"
        LV, 7, 0.0                  ! line 25 -INITIALIZE FIRST TIME
X104    LOC(SEOP), 0.0, 0.0         ! line 26 -POSITION TO ARC ZERO

! ---- DISK IO TEST, line 27's comment ------------------------------
X105    SIC, XERRAD                 ! line 28
        BEKJZ, XERROR               ! line 29 -IF EXCHANGE ERROR
XERR12  SIC, XERRAD                 ! line 30
        BUNRJZ, XERROR              ! line 31 -IF DISK NOT READY
XERR13  SIC, XERRAD                 ! line 32
        BCBJZ, XERROR               ! line 33 -IF DISK BUSY
        END, XIN
